# Host build output must never enter the build context: the image builds into its
# own directories, so ours is dead weight that gets re-sent and re-COPYed on every
# source edit.
#
# `build/` on its own matches ONLY the root build dir, so the nested ones were
# slipping through — lib/libnatkit-core/build is ~171M — and the whole tree is
# re-COPYed by the project layer every time a source file changes. Match at any
# depth instead. (Verified: the only directories named `build` in this tree are
# ./build, ./lib/libnatkit-core/build and ./third-party/drogon/build — all output.)
build/
**/build/
.cache/
uploads/
**/CMakeFiles/
**/CMakeCache.txt
